DESCRIPTION >
    AI Visibility — "Agents" view. Which crawlers fetched this site, how often,
    and how well each count is verified. Tenant-scoped; prunes via
    (site_id, timestamp), matching the datasource sorting key.

    Verification is NOT collapsed into a single "verified" number. Each row
    carries the counts split by verification state so the UI can render a
    UA-only count differently from an IP-verified one, per the requirement that
    the distinction live in the data model rather than in a reader's head.

    ip_mismatch is reported SEPARATELY and is excluded from `hits`: a request
    claiming to be GPTBot from outside OpenAI's published ranges is evidence of
    impersonation, not evidence of GPTBot, and adding it to the bot's total
    would overstate exactly the number the report exists to answer.

    NOT YET DEPLOYED — Tinybird pipe deploys are founder-gated (CLAUDE.md §8)
    and `tb --cloud deploy --check` is the mandatory pre-deploy gate. This file
    has NOT been run against a workspace.

NODE crawler_agents_node
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        bot_name,
        operator,
        category,
        countIf(verification != 'ip_mismatch')                     AS hits,
        countIf(verification = 'ip_verified')                      AS hits_ip_verified,
        countIf(verification = 'ua_only')                          AS hits_ua_only,
        countIf(verification = 'ua_only_no_ranges_published')      AS hits_ua_only_no_ranges,
        countIf(verification = 'ip_mismatch')                      AS hits_ip_mismatch,
        uniq(path)                                                 AS unique_paths,
        max(timestamp)                                             AS last_seen
    FROM crawler_hits
    WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
      AND timestamp >= {{ DateTime(from_ts, required=True) }}
      AND timestamp <= {{ DateTime(to_ts, required=True) }}
    GROUP BY bot_name, operator, category
    ORDER BY hits DESC
    LIMIT 200

TYPE endpoint
